# Product Rules

## What this is

REA-TEMPLATE is a reusable investigation workspace for official [REA](https://github.com/morluto/rea) (Reverse Engineer Anything). Clone [BOXELS/cursor-rules-rea](https://github.com/BOXELS/cursor-rules-rea) into any new investigation so Cursor already knows the workflow.

This folder is the starter: pick an authorized target, inspect it with REA, keep an evidence ledger, and optionally reconstruct a similar feature in `reconstructions/`.

## Who uses this

Primary user: an operator who chooses what to inspect and already has (or will state) authorization. They compare this to "open the app in Hopper/Ghidra and take notes," but the agent drives REA and writes the ledger.

## Key user flows

1. Authorize → name the target and path → start investigation notes → inspect with REA → write findings
2. Follow one feature through evidence → explain it in plain language → optionally reconstruct it for our own project
3. Update REA / refresh Cursor registration → resume from saved evidence, do not repeat identical analysis

Every new task should connect to one of these flows. If it doesn't, question whether it belongs in this workspace.

